! Turkish March -- Rondo alla Turca, from Piano Sonata No. 11, K. 331 iii
! W. A. Mozart (public domain). Score data: Mutopia Project edition
! (typeset by Rune Zedeler and Chris Sawer), taken from its MIDI file.
!
! Optimized version of turkish-march.factor: the rondo's repetitions
! are factored out. Of the 256 bars (128 per voice) only 122 are
! distinct; each distinct bar is defined once as a word, phrases are
! built from bar words with narray, and repeated phrases are reused
! through seq. The printed event list is identical to the original
! version (verified note for note: 1,614 events).
!
! An event is { start midi dur } in ticks (384 ticks = one quarter
! note), with start relative to its bar. Bar 0 is the 1-beat pickup;
! every later bar is 2 beats (2/4). Rests are the gaps between events.
USING: arrays io kernel locals math prettyprint sequences
    sequences.generalizations ;
IN: turkish-march

! --- combinators and score assembly ---
: seq ( seq seq -- seq ) append ;
: par ( voice voice -- voices ) 2array ;

: bar-offset ( index -- ticks )
    dup zero? [ drop 0 ] [ 768 * 384 - ] if ;

:: shift-event ( event offset -- event' )
    event first offset + event second event third 3array ;

:: shift-bar ( bar offset -- events )
    bar [ offset shift-event ] map ;

: voice-events ( voice -- events )
    [ bar-offset shift-bar ] map-index concat ;

: score-events ( voices -- events )
    [ voice-events ] map concat ;

